OXDK is released into the public domain.

Anyone is free to copy, modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute it,
by any means and for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial. No attribution
is required, though it is welcome. The tools and the patches exist to be
expanded and reused by whoever wants them.

This applies to the parts written for OXDK: the build system, the shims, the
tools under xbox/tools and xbox360/tools, the LLVM patches under xbox360/llvm,
the scripts, the samples, and the documentation.

It does not apply to everything in the tree.

Third party code keeps its own license. The vendored libraries under
xbox/third-party and xbox360/third-party carry their own terms, and the LLVM
patches are changes to LLVM, which is Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. The two
libc++ headers checked in under common/libcxx are copies of LLVM's own and
carry that same license. Anything you build with OXDK is yours and keeps
whatever license you give it.

Microsoft's XDK is not here and is not ours to give. You supply your own.

